      "answer": "A provision is a liability created for an expense or loss whose amount or timing is not yet certain, by debiting an expense and crediting the provision. Examples: Provision for Bad Debts / Doubtful Debts, Provision for Discount on Debtors, and Provision for Repairs and Renewals. Provisions are charges against profit and are made even in a loss year."
