      "q": "What is a Reserve? State two features of a reserve.",
      "answer": "A reserve is an amount kept OUT OF PROFIT for a future need or for strengthening the business. Features: (i) it can be created only out of available profit — it is an appropriation, not a charge; (ii) it is shown on the liabilities side under Reserves & Surplus and belongs to the proprietor, so it increases the owner's claim on the business."
