      "q": "Explain the main points of difference between a Provision and a Reserve.",
      "answer": "(i) Meaning: a provision is a liability of uncertain amount or timing; a reserve is a division of profit kept aside for future use. (ii) Creation: a provision is created by debiting an expense before net profit is struck; a reserve is created by appropriating profit already arrived at. (iii) Necessity: a provision must be made whenever an expected loss exists, even in a loss year; a reserve can be created only when there is profit. (iv) Purpose: a provision recognises an expected outflow; a reserve strengthens the financial position or funds a future programme."
