      "answer": "A provision is a CHARGE AGAINST PROFIT — it must be recorded whenever there is an expected loss or liability, irrespective of whether the business earns a profit, because the matching concept requires the expected loss of the period to be recognised now. So the ₹25,000 provision is recorded (and it actually deepens the loss). A reserve, on the other hand, is an APPROPRIATION of profit — since there is no profit this year, nothing can be appropriated, and creating a 'reserve' would be arithmetically impossible and conceptually wrong."
