      "answer": "When debtors are given with an old provision and a new provision is required, three steps are followed. Step 1 — remove the bad debts from debtors: Remaining Debtors = Debtors − Bad Debts. Step 2 — compute the new provision on the remaining debtors at the given rate: New Provision = Remaining Debtors × Rate. Step 3 — the amount charged to the P&L A/c = Bad Debts + New Provision − Old Provision (this is the increase in the charge, since the old provision already lying in the books is released). In the Balance Sheet, debtors are shown at Remaining Debtors − New Provision. Example: Debtors ₹80,000, Bad Debts ₹2,000, old provision ₹1,000, new provision @5%: remaining = ₹78,000; new provision = ₹3,900; charge to P&L = 2,000 + 3,900 − 1,000 = ₹4,900; debtors shown = 78,000 − 3,900 = ₹74,100."
